  <title>Language switching</title>
  <p>
    Language switching lets you change the voice used for different languages. Orca can switch
    automatically based on language information provided by the application, or you can switch
    manually using keyboard commands.
  </p>
  <p>
    Manual language selection takes precedence over automatic switching. Returning to the global
    voice set restores automatic switching. The settings and commands below control these
    options; see "<link xref="features_speech_and_voices_voice_sets">Voice sets</link>" to configure the
    voices themselves.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-language-switching">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Speech</gui> category, <gui>Global Voice Settings</gui> group.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Language Switching</gui>: Controls when Orca
          switches voices based on language.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Document content</gui>: Controls automatic
              language switching for document content. For example, disable it in global
              preferences but enable it in application preferences for one or more web browsers.
              Other applications continue to use the global setting unless they have their own
              override. See "<link xref="preferences_guide">Preferences</link>" for opening global
              and application preferences and removing overrides. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>UI elements</gui>: Automatically
              switch voice based on UI element language. Default: off.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Limit switching to configured voices</gui>: Limits automatic
              switching to languages for which you have configured a voice set. With this limit
              off, Orca can use any language supported by the synthesizer, even without a
              matching voice set. Default: off.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
  <section id="commands-voice-sets">
    <title>Commands</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Speech and verbosity</gui> group.
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Cycle to the next voice set</gui>: Unbound by
          default.
        </p>
        <p>
          Cycles through configured voice sets. Selecting a language-specific voice set manually
          suspends automatic language switching until you return to the global voice set.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Switch voice to: Global</gui>: Unbound by
          default.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
